# RTL + Tailwind UI conventions (novavilla)

## Height

Do not set `h-*`, `min-h-*`, or fixed height on blocks that already have padding + text/content. Content defines height naturally.

Use explicit height only when the element has no text flow (e.g. image wrapper: `w-full h-64 sm:h-72` + `object-cover` on the img — no `aspect-*` or arbitrary ratio px).

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD — fixed height on a padded text row -->
<div class="flex items-center justify-between h-8 rounded-lg px-3 py-1">...</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<div class="flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg px-3 py-1">...</div>
```

## RTL alignment

Site is Persian (RTL). Do **not** add `justify-end`, `self-end`, `text-end`, or similar end-alignment utilities unless Figma clearly requires it for that node. In RTL they often flip alignment and break right-to-left layout.

Default block/inline flow and `justify-between` are enough for most cards.

## Transitions

Prefer `transition-all duration-300` — not `transition-colors` alone.

```html
<a class="group ... transition-all duration-300">
```

## Text size — Tailwind scale, not arbitrary px

Map Figma px to nearest Tailwind utility:

| Figma (approx.) | Use |
|-----------------|-----|
| ~11px | `text-xs` |
| ~13–14px | `text-sm` |
| ~16px | `text-base` |

Avoid `text-[13px]` etc. unless no close match or a one-off design exception.

```html
<!-- ❌ -->
<span class="text-[13px] leading-[13px]">...</span>

<!-- ✅ -->
<span class="text-sm">...</span>
```

## Border radius — Tailwind scale, not arbitrary px

Pick the **nearest Tailwind step upward** (round up), same logic as font sizes.

| Figma (approx.) | Use |
|-----------------|-----|
| ~4px | `rounded-sm` |
| ~8px | `rounded-lg` |
| ~12px | `rounded-xl` |
| ~16px | `rounded-2xl` |
| ~20–24px | `rounded-3xl` |
| ~28–32px | `rounded-4xl` |

Avoid `rounded-[20px]` etc. unless no close match or a one-off exception.

```html
<!-- ❌ -->
<div class="rounded-[20px] ...">

<!-- ✅ -->
<div class="rounded-3xl ...">
```
